# Response headers for a Workers Static Assets tree.
#
# `_headers` is parsed by Workers and is never served as an asset itself. Every
# tree copies this file to its asset root, so it holds only rules that are true
# both in development and in production.
#
# CORS: a generated page may be hosted on any origin, so the bundle has to be
# loadable cross-origin. Module scripts are fetched in CORS mode, which is why
# this is required and not merely a convenience.
#
# Cache rules for releases are deliberately *not* here. `scripts/build-release.ts`
# appends them per release, with the policy of that release: long-lived caching for
# a published version, revalidation for the debug release, which is overwritten in
# place. The development tree gets none of them, because it serves the same
# versioned URL while `vite build --watch` rewrites it: an immutable response there
# would leave the browser on a stale bundle with no revalidation.
/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
